.TH OECTL 8 "November 2026" "OpenEIGRP" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
oectl \- OpenEIGRP native Linux control client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oectl
.RI [ options ] " show " view
.br
.B oectl
.RI [ options ] " clear events"
.br
.B oectl
.RI [ options ] " version"
.br
.B oectl help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oectl
connects to the local
.B openeigrpd
Unix control socket using the versioned management protocol. It is a
non-interactive, one-shot operational client. It does not read or alter
EIGRP core objects directly.
.PP
Read-only requests require access to the daemon socket, normally granted
through its group (mode 0660). The daemon checks peer credentials and
permits the sole mutating operation, clear events, only to root or the
UID that started the management service. Running
.B oectl
as root is not required for read-only commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show capabilities
Portable release and AF/TLV feature availability.
.TP
.B show protocols
Configured protocol instances, including runtime state.
.TP
.B show neighbors
Neighbor state, hold time, queues, retransmissions and uptime.
.TP
.B show interfaces
EIGRP interface configuration and runtime counters.
.TP
.B show topology
DUAL prefix and path snapshots.
.TP
.B show routes
Successor and feasible paths in the EIGRP topology view. This does not
query the Linux kernel routing table.
.TP
.B show statistics
Portable EIGRP traffic statistics. 
.B show traffic
is an alias.
.TP
.B show events
Event ring summary and entries.
.TP
.B show diagnostics
Feature capabilities, debug state and timer records.
.TP
.B show tech-support
Report integration version, daemon capabilities and protocols, then
available read-only views for running default-VRF instances. Scoped options
limit it to one instance. 
.B tech-support
is an alias. Explicit selectors are required for nondefault VRFs.
.TP
.B clear events
Clear the event ring for the selected running instance. Requires daemon
administrator credentials. No other mutation is supported by IPC v1.
.TP
.B version
Display local integration release, OS, distribution, kernel, architecture,
and management protocol version without requiring the daemon.
.TP
.B show version
Display local version data and query the daemon for the portable release.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-s, --socket " path
Absolute Unix socket path (default: /run/openeigrpd/control.sock).
.TP
.BI "-a, --asn " n
EIGRP autonomous system, 1 through 65535.
.TP
.BR -4 , " -6" , " --afi 4|6"
Address family. With no family specified, select a unique running instance.
.TP
.BI "--vrf-id " n
Numeric runtime VRF ID (default 0). For a nonzero VRF, supply both
.B --asn
and
.BR --afi .
.TP
.B --json
Emit newline-delimited JSON records for machine consumption, including
tech-support. The client adds integration and scope records to the latter.
Daemon field names and data follow the management IPC protocol.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage. 
.B --version
prints the local integration version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success, 1 for daemon, authorization, selection or protocol failures,
2 for invalid command-line input. A missing or stopped daemon is reported
on standard error with its socket pathname.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Protocol v1 uses 16-byte request selectors and 16-KiB, 32-record pages.
No stable snapshot is guaranteed across pages; concurrent topology changes
may change results. The current daemon restricts the page offset to 8192,
so larger state dumps stop with an error rather than silently succeed.
Tech-support cannot discover numeric IDs of nondefault VRFs from the
current protocol listing; explicitly select these instances.
.SH SEE ALSO
openeigrpd.conf(5)
